What the Apache license covers
------------------------------
The original work in this repository: the specification, the decision
register and the other documents under drafts/; the handbook, kernel
schema, standard-library facet descriptors, conformance corpus, example
bundle and software under jascon/; the reader under one-page-apps/; and
the coverage reports under converted_examples/.

What it does not cover: converted third-party publications
----------------------------------------------------------
Each bundle (and OSCAL re-export) under converted_examples/ is a
conversion of a publication by its authority and is offered under that
publication's terms, stated in the SOURCE-LICENSE.md beside it. Terms
were read in the publishers' own repositories on 2026-11-10.

  AU.ISM           Information Security Manual, Australian Signals
                   Directorate. (c) Commonwealth of Australia.
                   CC BY 4.0.
  DE.BSI           Anwenderkatalog Grundschutz++, Bundesamt fuer
                   Sicherheit in der Informationstechnik (BSI).
                   CC BY-SA 4.0 - the converted bundle is ShareAlike
                   material and is itself CC BY-SA 4.0.
  US.SP800-53      NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5.2.0 / 800-53A / 800-53B.
  US.CSF           NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0.
  US.IFA-GoodRead  NIST OSCAL example content (fictional).
                   All three: U.S. public domain, CC0 1.0 worldwide.
  FedRAMP-CR26     FedRAMP Consolidated Rules for 2026, U.S. General
                   Services Administration. A work of the U.S.
                   Government (17 U.S.C. 105); the publisher's
                   repository states no licence.

The example bundle under jascon/examples/ is illustrative. Its requirement
KONF.14.1 paraphrases one requirement of the Grundschutz++ catalogue (BSI,
CC BY-SA 4.0); the other requirement texts are invented.

Measured, not redistributed
---------------------------
Five further corpora were converted and measured, and their bundles were
removed from this repository on 2026-11-10 because the publishers' terms
forbid redistributing an adapted form or could not be established:
CIS Controls v8.1 and the CIS Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS Benchmark (Center
for Internet Security - terms forbid derivative works and re-posting),
BSI C5:2026, BSI C3A v1.0, and the CCB CyberFundamentals Framework 2025
(no licence statement found). Their converters and coverage reports
remain; each directory's NOT-REDISTRIBUTED.md gives the reason.

